  "question": {
    ":question/id": "761aa371-9571-5d54-bc00-dfd0892e1756",
    ":question/problem": "Find $PQ,$ if\n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$Q=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Here, $P$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix and $Q$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $P$ and $1$ row in matrix $Q$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{P}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{Q}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={PQ}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 0 & 1\\cdot 4 \\\\ (-10)\\cdot 0 & (-10)\\cdot 4 \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & 0\\cdot 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -40 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
